  <!-- The exemptions the aggregate above requires (#171).

       AggregateWith INHERITS, so merging it onto a vanilla parent reaches every vanilla
       DESCENDANT of that parent as well - not only this fork's variants. Without these ten,
       Hulking Baboon, Shrewd Baboon and Baboon Hero 1 fold into Baboon's single slot and baboons
       in the hills go from four slots to one; ClockworkBeetle, which is a machine, competes for
       the giant beetle's slot; and Sultan Croc shares the ordinary croc's. That shipped, and it
       took a playtest to notice, because nothing about it errors.

       *delete is vanilla's own idiom for dropping an inherited tag, used on AggregateWith twice
       in the base game. Each of these keeps the spawn slot vanilla gave it.

       This list is not maintained by hand. tools/qud-api.json records every vanilla descendant of
       an aggregated parent, and validate_mod.py's `aggregate-sweep` check fails until each one is
       exempted - so a future Qud patch adding a descendant to one of these six families turns up
       as a red run rather than as quietly rarer baboons. -->

